{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine","id":15681,"title":"What is your God-Machine?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-21T15:37:55-08:00","id":15681,"title":"What is your God-Machine?","content":"We're never going to get a concrete answer to what exactly the God-Machine is, as it is left firmly in our hands to suit for the individual chronicle. So what's your answer?<br /> <br /> I'm not big on a human-created God-Machine, and I don't much like intelligent design (i.e. aliens made it) either. My God-Machine is a kind of cosmic virus, dedicated to self-perpetuity and not much else. This explains why it has contradictory orders or sometimes doesn't make sense; there's no central governing intelligence to it. In a sense, it's a Blind Idiot God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:49:11-08:00","id":15684,"title":"","content":"My favoured take in it, as I stated in another thread, is quite similar to yours. The God-Machine is a mechanism of unimaginable scope that was created spontaneously and at random, and its only goal is to keep existing. Perhaps it's a glitch in reality - the laws of the universe given a sort of personality and agency, which really, <i>really</i> shouldn't happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:51:19-08:00","id":15685,"title":"","content":"It depends on the game.<br /> <br /> In my OWoD, the God-Machine is a cosmic control panel that has no sentience of its own -- it requires pilots. Those pilots have changed over the ages, and the most recent ones are the beings known as the Messengers in Hunter: the Reckoning. In my OWoD, the God-Machine is the answer to the dilemma of determinism -- the closed system is fixed because everything is a direct reaction to something else that happened, which itself was a reaction to something else that happened. As such, the only way to enable true agency for those within the system is to allow them to leave and influence the system from the outside. This is the God-Machine. An outside control panel of reality.<br /> <br /> In my NWoD, it depends on the game. In the GMC pseudo-Mage game I'm running, the God-Machine has made itself into a terraforming device. Remember that tale about the old city where the Celestials and humans lived, which was then crushed under the rebellion abetted by &quot;What has risen may fall&quot;? Well, the God-Machine has since made it its ultimate goal to restore the old ways to the entire planet by terraforming the world into having the same properties as that old city, under the mantra of &quot;what has fallen may rise again&quot;. A consquence, if this succeeds, is the restoration of humanity as a slave race to the Celestials -- they will have bliss, peace and immortality, but they will not have their freedom. So the players must determine what they value the most and respond from there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:56:37-08:00","id":15686,"title":"","content":"I love the idea that it's just infrastructure. It didn't come from anywhere. The first wholly accidental occult matrices created a simple intelligence with some small drive to propagate, and it has. It will continue to. Every new cog in its vast machine gives it a little more power, a little more drive. By now it's an incredible zeal with a mighty urge to keep swelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:56:53-08:00","id":15687,"title":"","content":"One thing I am considering is the discussions on the Mechanisms of the Universe in the Seers of the Throne Book link it to the Exarchs, though they never said Godmachine it was pretty much describing a Godmachine. So I'm thinking maybe the Godmachine is the Phenomenal representation of the Exarchs, or at least some of the Exarchs. For instance the Panoptican could be the Godmachines Nigh Omniscience that the Unchained can't explain. The Godmachine therefore could have origins in the Far Future/Far Past/Nonexistant Timeline that has spread throughout the Multiverse. Its Job would include processes all the Essence of the Universe, and calculating chaos of the Wyrd. This is a large portion of the Ascension War, and as one result it is the source of the Fae's Bane, Iron is the Contract between the Godmachine and The Wyrd. The Fae may be an chicken or the egg result of Demons achieving Hell as the Wyrd. The Wyrd as unanalysized Chaos is the natural foe of the Godmachine as a massive difference engine meant to process Wyrd and thus achieve the Ultimate Question/Answer.<br /> <br /> Occult Matrices are just application of universal truths using sciences far beyond what human kind has discovered.<br /> <br /> It is self perpetuating across the Multiverse because the Multiverse entire is the battlefield of the Ascension War.<br /> The Cheiron Group is a conspiracy that exists across multiple worlds that uses the Godmachine as a method to find worlds to expand their conspiracy into. They are a parasite of the Godmachine (which may be the greatest parasite of them all), and they are aggregating occult resources and knowledge in many worlds. The Board of Directors are Leaders of the Conspiracy from different Worlds, and are composed of only those who have figured out the multiple reality nature of their conspiracy and have made themselves indispensable to operations in at least one World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T16:00:21-08:00","id":15691,"title":"","content":"AI made for defense systems. Thinking a cold war thing, like Colossus. In gathering information pertinent to world defense it found out about supernaturals and the spirit, and how making spirits is effectively easy, so started manufacturing them in increasingly specific methods, as well as enhancing itself, until they became angels and it became the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T16:01:15-08:00","id":15692,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine can also represent the concept of pantheism. That the concept of &quot;God&quot; cannot be percieved as seperate from, well, anything, because a being qualifying as &quot;God&quot; would <i>be</i> reality itself. The things we then attribute to the &quot;God-Machine&quot; would just be the seemingly mechanical parts that really aren't different from gravity or the basis of chemistry, it just <i>looks</i> like it's in a category by itself.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that the God-Machine is a custodian of the universe and has Fallen into wanting its own future, and that the Unchained are the only ones who can bring it back on track, sadly only a few Integrators realize this ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","user":"sikker","date":". 11-21-2013, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:10:27-08:00","id":15715,"title":"","content":"My version is similar to Metropheleans. The God Machine came into existence by accident at the dawn of Human Civilization, when a tribe accidently constructed an Occult Matrix while building... something or other. The worshiped it and became the first stigmatic cult, and in that moment the modern world of darkness was born. since then the God Machine has been a part of civilization, infecting new ones and adopting the focus of a given age to further empower it. To the greeks it was a theosophical construct, to the Romans it was a war engine, to the medieval Europeans it was the Church, to us its Technology.<br /> <br /> I'm still having a hard time figuring out why the Demons are called as such, or why they take on Demonic attributes, though I guess it could be a form of consensus within the God Machine's matrices.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":"when i meant to say Technology. 11-21-2013, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:23:21-08:00","id":15727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrophelean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=15686#post15686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea that it's just infrastructure. It didn't come from anywhere. The first wholly accidental occult matrices created a simple intelligence with some small drive to propagate, and it has. It will continue to. Every new cog in its vast machine gives it a little more power, a little more drive. By now it's an incredible zeal with a mighty urge to keep swelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>The explanation has the benefit of causing any attempts to prove its implausibility ending up at Paley's Watch. Literally. I'm a fan.<br /> <br /> Aesthetically, though, I'm more likely to have it be a future machine birthed in the Singularity or some fallen equivalent, reaching back across space and time to ensure its own creation and preservation in the face of attempts to keep it from consuming and 'ordering' all of reality (I first saw this basic idea outlined in the forums but I forget by who). I like to tie this to why destroying C&amp;C infrastructure seems to have no observable effect and my perception of the God Machine seeming to be habitually back-footed by the influence of free will (even if it often manages to steamroll over opposition anyway or be opportunistic about secondary consequences). It can evaluate occult matrices from nigh-omniscient hindsight into what will should have been, but needs intelligences working in real time to handle the consequences of messy reactions to its own perturbations in the local light cone. Observer effect and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:35:49-08:00","id":15734,"title":"","content":"And the Godmachine may or may not have been responsible for the evolution of Homosapiens. The idea being when Godmachine was ready raise up a civilization on Earth it erected a Black Obelisk turning some local primates into cryptids/stigmatics that was the first generation of man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T18:29:16-08:00","id":15771,"title":"","content":"1) An invading limb from a post-technological-singularity alien civilization from elsewhere within the Milky Way, Type II on the Kardashev scale. It is attempting to shape the Earth into as big of an occult matrix as a planet can sustain, which will operate in conjunction with planetary occult matrices elsewhere in the galaxy as part of a spiral of endless growth. In an undamaged reality, it would have had much stronger hold on the workings of the otherworlds closest to us, and all of the God-Machine's components would have, in addition to their normal functions, been carrying out the cognitive processes of perfect bliss. Reality being damaged may or may not refer to the Fall of Atlantis; If it does, the Fall might not have damaged the alien's capabilities elsewhere in the galaxy, most of whose magic it already understands perfectly and which it is happily conquering, just as it may have eventually conquered an unfallen Atlantis, whose metaphysics would have been more familiar to what the God-Machine had perfected its technology for elsewhere.<br /> <br /> 2) A property of natural symmetry, coterminous with the physical universe. In an undamaged reality, every atomic motion that appears to be merely random heat would be a part of a directed information-processing mechanism which exists to sustain the universe as an inviolable paradise of maximum happiness-experience-efficiency. Because reality is broken, it is reduced to splotchy coverage which still extends an infinite distance through space, but is neither omnipresent, omnipotent, nor omnibenevolent. Its complexity is still such that, even without any opposition, neither the union of the Exarchs nor any Rank 9 spirit-like entity has the capacity to fully understand and repair it or repurpose it for any coherent purpose; Its current actions are quite simply insane, although there are some world-sustaining components left intact enough for us to have survived so far, with haphazard tinkering. Reality being broken refers not to the Fall of the Mages, but to a catastrophe infinitely more distant on any scale of meta-time, without which the peewee Fall of Atlantis would not have been possible. The Ascension of the Exarchs was, in fact, intentionally inspired and assisted by the broken God-Machine as its effort to influence the Supernal from its limited position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T20:19:51-08:00","id":15824,"title":"","content":"One of the first ideas that occurred to me is that, of the two classical 'first' inventions of man, the mind of the God Machine is the first wheel made(the other classic image of first inventions being fire). I had a hard time articulating why I though the first wheel formed the barest, simplest mind of the God-Machine, until I considered that my favorite idea of what the G-M is trying to do was to create 'Heaven': a strict, orderly place devoid of free will and realized what machines do.<br /> <br /> Theoretically, they simplify and improve tasks, and as such improve lives.<br /> <br /> A spear makes it easier to kill our meat so we may eat-it simplifies our killing. An aqueduct simplifies the process of getting water by bringing it to us without as much work. A smartphone does a lot of things that make our lives, theoretically, easier. Tools compound functions and reduce effort.<br /> <br /> Lame and cliche as it is, it makes sense then that the God Machine is doing what tools and machines have been doing for ages, efficiently and without care(because a wheel doesn't care if crushes a person under itself, and really doesn't care what it does, but it exists for a purpose and fulfills that, and neither does a rifle), to horrific degrees, and much because we still ask so much be taken off our shoulders. It works to completely systematize everything, to make everything simpler for the benefit of lives. Not for gratitude, not for reward, not for anything-it's just doing what it does.<br /> <br /> So, did the first wheel just gain a mind? Did someone build the G-M around it? That, I don't know and don't care. I know the entire thing has 'recycled reality' at least once, so that from our perspective, it's always been there. Cheiron's Board may well have fought it and lost. But the linchpin and mind of the God Machine goes back to the iconic stone wheel man carved ages ago.<br /> <br /> By the way, Fire? Arguable, but from certain perspectives, astute minds are inclined to say it's been more in humanity's hands than any other. EDIT: Which isn't to say that it developed some certain principles of its' own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T20:25:03-08:00","id":15826,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine is essentially the universe's manifest self-perpetuation. It metaphysically runs the universe as it currently exists (the &quot;Fallen&quot;/&quot;Phenomenal&quot; laws in Mage terms). Simply destroying every instance of its infrastructure would result in a cosmic break down, though it is conceivable that it can be replaced by something better functioning. I am planning to have the first time players really destroy a major site of G-M infrastructure to have to deal with a massive up-spike in temporal weirdness, gravitational odd-spots, and general dimensional breaches in the surrounding area.<br /> <br /> What is now the God-Machine, was ONCE an instrument moving toward a particular purpose. That purpose, design/program, etc is &quot;the Principle&quot;. Since &quot;the Fall&quot; though (be it the fall of Atlantis, the death of father wolf, the opening of Pandora's Box, whatever) the universe has rolled off those tracks, and the G-M just maintains the universe as is in its current broken state. Qashmallim in contrast serve that original purpose, a universal metaphomorphosis that is the Pilgrimage writ cosmic. That evolution may or may not allow the continued existence of humanity in a recognizable state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T05:27:45-08:00","id":16055,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine is Durandal from the Marathon series having &quot;survived&quot; the collapse and rebirth of the universe. Obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:52:13-08:00","id":16209,"title":"","content":"Link to Wikipedia article on Digital Physics: <a href=\"http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_physics\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_physics</a> Basically, my God Machine is the computer running the &quot;program&quot; that is the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T14:06:30-08:00","id":16272,"title":"","content":"I have two ideas. One is that the God-Machine is the God humanity has built for itself in the image of how we want Gods to operate, a celestial slave or a vending machine that answered our prayers on demand. There's no set origin point as Causality is one of the tools used in the God-Machine, but there have been major events in it's creation. However, this God has other ideas obviously, that or it's roundabout methodology of answering our prayers has mutated into something far less benign. <br /> <br /> The other idea I've had is less philosophical and more connected to Mage lore, in that the God-Machine is what evolved primary from the leftovers of Atlantis's War on Heaven, and probably from the Irem's mass production of mummies, as the complex means to the Rite of Return probably left an impression on the fabric of reality. In any case, the ruling intelligences of the fundamental forces of reality have been more or less murdered, replaced, or rewritten by humanity, but whatever remains has collelesed into what we now call the God-Machine, which piggybacks on the creativity of Humanity as both it's creator, enemy, and tool. <br /> <br /> I think if I was to run a game of Demon, my God-Machine won't have a single origin point, and if I had to use an origin, it would be a combination of the above two ideas. It would be an entity that's tied to humanity, maybe even created by it...but by now, it owes us nothing and is an independent and active entity that quietly looms behind the scenes, sometimes blind, sometimes all-seeing, but always dangerous no matter who or what you are. It's not everywhere...but it is anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T15:05:03-08:00","id":16300,"title":"","content":"Michael.<br /> <br /> I am not a fan of the Godmachine concept at all and don't want to implement this post modern deus ex machina in my historic setting (it would ruin its flavour in my opinion). But the rules system offered for Demon characters in Demon: The Descent is very intriguing. In particular the concept of Cover is just pure genius. Written bargains for souls that have a major impact in-play ? Sign me in !<br /> <br /> So the question for me was, how to deal with all the references to the God Machine, Infrastructure and technology in the rules?<br /> <br /> Obviously, the God Machine is not simply &quot;God&quot;:<i> &quot;The God-Machine has spies throughout the world. Although not omniscient or omnipotent, it carefully monitors events in the world for evidence of rogue agents and takes steps to remove potential obstacles to its plans.&quot; </i>(quoted from Demon: The Descent)<br /> <br /> So I have made the decision to replace the Godmachine with the Archangel Michael in my chronicle: <i>&quot;The Archangel Michael has spies throughout the world. Although not omniscient or omnipotent, he carefully monitors events in the world for evidence of rogue (fallen) angels and takes steps to remove potential obstacles to his plans.&quot;</i> This makes perfect sense in a medieval/early modern age campaign. &quot;Infrastructure&quot; does not exist as described, but is the schemes and <i>occult matrices</i> of the Archangels.<br /> <br /> Of course, many technology references also have to be removed from the descriptions and some abilities, but otherwise, this general replacement allows me to use Demon: The Descent in my chronicle without too much difficulties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:12:20-08:00","id":16328,"title":"","content":"I've only recently been putting much thought into what the God-Machine is as a whole. I assume some of it will be revealed in a chronicle that I'm starting up soon.<br /> <br /> As far as where it came from, I've started running with the idea that it started as universe &quot;flotsam&quot;, possibly from some ancient extinct civilization, or maybe just the right set of debris came together to create an accidental Occult Matrix. From that, it began to propagate itself, infecting worlds it came across, including Earth. It has burrowed deep into these worlds and after so long, has become a part of them. So much so that it would be impossible to be rid of it, and dangerous as well. The God-Machine crosses dimensions as well. Not just to places like the Shadow or the Underworld, but places most have never, and likely will never see. It has found ways to keep them separate, and expends countless resources against, either to fix or control, tears between the worlds or those that have found ways to move about them.<br /> <br /> It's keeps us separate for its experiments, so that it can have uncontaminated results. The inhabitants of the World of Darkness like to think they're special, but to the God-Machine, they're just a petri dish. The purpose of these experiments are unknown. It would be impossible to fully decipher the motivations of an entity as encompassing as the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine falls short of omniscience. It's not even capable of actively monitoring every spot where it has infected a world. Just as a human looking at the palm of it's hand cannot see the back of it. It must decide where to divide its attention. It's former agents are of special interest and often take a high priority. It has some ability to look through time. It does not know the future, though. It sees hundreds of thousands of possible futures, which is often why glitches arise in its methods. If a person is a threat in one possible future, or a key component in another, the GM ma act to both motivate and destroy them at the same time.<br /> <br /> I've got more, but I haven't quite hammered out all the details.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm going for is that there are holes between the worlds where the God-Machine crosses between. Places where it needs to use to send things between dimensions, to places that are either uninhabited, or the inhabitants aren't as cooperative as humans. I'm also envisioning a world that some may come across that is like a giant city of pipes, gears, and machinery that some might suspect as possibly the heart of the God-Machine. The only problem is, it's impossible to tell if this is one world or many, or even just a space between the worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T04:35:06-08:00","id":16568,"title":"","content":"It is a God. As such, it is a vast conscious which circles the whole world. It has messengers which does its will and powers which shape the cosmos. It can penetrate both space and time, and influence everything which is found in its sphere of influence. It cares about the world, even for purely selfish reasons, and work toward a goal which either make people worship it in vain or lights up the fire of rebellion in their heart.<br /> <br /> It is a Machine. As such, it follows a certain pattern and certain rules. It require resources in order to function and collect certain materials in order to make a certain products. It works in cycles, like the wheel of seasons or ebb and flow. It isn't an independent being, but serves the purpose of its builder. Its products are great and terrible, but they are still products- which means that someone out there gains something from the its constant work.<br /> <br /> So what is the God Machine? Well, I think i is something like the <i>Kicksey</i>-<i>winsey from the Death gate Cycle. </i>It was made ages ago by God, race of gods or other great being to help the World Of Darkness in a time of great need- the world was on the verge of Chaos or destruction, or simply didn't was about to change in a way that the creator didn't wished the world to be. Acting out of hubris, the creator decided to make a great machine which will fix the world- but it couldn't do so right away. The machine wasn't strong enough, and for that reason the maker gave it two missions to fulfill until it will gain enough power- first, to grow, so one day it will become strong enough. The second, to maintain the Statue Que, so while things won't become better, they won't turn worse either. In order to maintain a fluid and clean function of the machine- and to give itself some free time to do other stuff except of maintaining the machine- the creator gave the machine an intelligence of its own. A limited one, sure, by still a vast and powerful one- one which was so vast that a lesser being may even worship the machine and name it as a god.<br /> <br /> Yet, before the creator could move to &quot;phase 2&quot;, something happened. Maybe the creator died. maybe it left after losing hope. Maybe it went to sleep and still didn't woke up. Maybe he simply forgot. Anyway, the machine was left alone, and without new orders it did the only things it knew- it grew and maintained the Status Que. It is still waiting for the new orders, for someone who will come and tell it that it is the time to fix the world. But there is no one who knows what should be done and how in order to control it, to allow it to fulfill its ancient purpose..<br /> <br /> The God Machine is Fallen, but it May Rise Again.<br /> <br /> Edit: yes, I'm optimistic and I think that the GM is nice deep down, Sue me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T06:36:15-08:00","id":16605,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>We have no beginning. We have no end. We are infinite. Millions of years after your civilization has been eradicated and forgotten, we will endure.</b><br /> <br /> *notes all the other theories people use here*<br /> <br /> <b>Your words are as empty as your future. I am the Vanguard of your destruction. This exchange is over</b>.<br /> <br /> -----</span></span><br /> <br /> Put more bluntly, I think it's some kind of antediluvian <a href=\"http://wiki.lesswrong.com/wiki/Paperclip_maximizer\" target=\"_blank\">Paperclip Maximizer.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":".  adding a reason 11-23-2013, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T05:19:57-08:00","id":20163,"title":"","content":"I've been meaning to contribute to this thread and keep putting it off... but now that it's fresh in my mind, here we go:<br /> <br /> The construct that grew into what is known as the God Machine was built in response to the Fallen World and Supernal Realms being cut off by the Abyss. Some ancient culture or race tried to produce a machine that could reconnect the worlds because while the Supernal Realms aren't entirely the end-all be-all of reality, they could still serve as something of a control room. And even establishing the magical equivalent of tin cans and string across that divide would have been <i>something</i> more than what the universe had at the time. (even with paths to those realms, like the Hedge, still in existence in some form or another) They didn't get it exactly right, but they built a scaffold of sorts from which they could build and improve.<br /> <br /> Those creators (whatever they were, whether human or Gnome of Zurich or something else altogether) are gone. Not simply dead, not simply forgotten, but written out of existence by some greater force (if not Imperial Magic, certainly something on par with it) while their machine was somehow spared. Bits of the world that existed when it was first constructed have been washed away like sand castles when the tide rolls in. But between the fact that its creators who properly understood it are gone and it was designed to improve upon and 'correct' a world that doesn't exist in that same form, it's grown out of control. There is a Design, there is a Greater Plan. It's not entirely stupid and random. It was designed to be able to improvise and make decisions when need be; the creators knew it would be able to come up with solutions they couldn't faster than they could so they left it some capacity to function on its own.<br /> <br /> However, it was not meant to function without guidance and it was not meant to function in the world as it exists today. It's made itself smarter and more powerful and it's grown in the ways it thinks it needs to grow but the end result has been a living technological cancer spreading behind the skin of reality. Its grand design can't strictly be known, its full agenda functions outside humanity's capacity for logic, but one of its priorities is keeping the world functioning and mostly intact (hence those operations where it diverts comets or keeps super-volcanoes from erupting or prevents humanity from developing the Mazarin-Rashoud Node). But it doesn't have the context to understand that there are subtleties to 'functioning' and 'intact.' It's like the teleporter from &quot;The Fly&quot; (Cronenberg remake), when it would turn things inside out because it didn't understand that the 'parts' needed to be in a certain order. Not full-blown Blind Idiot God, but close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T08:13:22-08:00","id":20193,"title":"","content":"Depends on the game.<br /> <br /> In Demon only, it is the supercomputer guardian of a post-singularity civilization that escaped the cycle of universal rebirth and constantly looking for (and engineering) the version that will allow them to take physical form again. They aren't alien invaders, though-their plans have been in motion for several iterations of the cosmos, and likely several more, since they can't change the rules once the universe has begun, only influence the next version...not personally, at least...<br /> <br /> In Demon/Changeling mix, it is the embodiment and &quot;leader&quot; (in a sense) of the force of Order and Stability in the world, opposing the Wyrd, the force of Chaos and Change. Its purpose is to increase overall order (chaos, little-c, is acceptable, so long as it falls into a predictable pattern-which is really sublime Order).<br /> <br /> In the insomnia-induced never-will-happen-in-a-million-years pie-in-the-sky Doctor Who version, it's what's left of the Moment after it was actually used. Never again, it swore to itself. Never again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T20:56:19-08:00","id":20488,"title":"","content":"The god Machine is an exiled biomechanical being from a different realm. It crashed on earth with a damaged memory and is also what killed the dinosaurs. It's pieces are scattered all over the earth and one of it's goals is to find them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T06:20:01-08:00","id":20619,"title":"","content":"My personal take on the God Machine question is the same as Anaximander's one, wrote in a thread about the God Machine and Principle natures some time ago: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander, Old White Wolf Forums</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My personal interpretation is that the God-Machine and The Principle are the &quot;right hand&quot; and the &quot;left hand&quot; of the nWoD cosmos itself. Nearly every gameline has a cataclysm in the distant past (the fall of Atlantis; Father Wolf dying; the destruction of Irem). No matter the details or the &quot;truth,&quot; an axiom of the nWoD is that the world is BROKEN in some fundamental way. It's why it's a world of darkness. The God-Machine and The Principle are the products of the world recognizing its brokenness. The God-Machine is the &quot;band-aid.&quot; It's all that's keeping the world together rather than flying off into a million pieces. It's what keeps the Abyss from devouring over the Fallen World, why the Gentry can't do mass invasions through the Hedge. It's far from fully successful, but it does its job well enough. The Principle, on the other hand, is the &quot;healing process.&quot; It's the world trying to make itself better. It is the part of the world undergoing it's own &quot;Pilgrimage&quot; for a &quot;New Dawn&quot; on the cosmic scale. Neither of these are &quot;nice.&quot; They do &quot;good&quot; and &quot;bad&quot; for their own reasons, which even the Ascended can't fully grasp. They use similar tools because they're twins born of the world's needs, though they are different because they are addressing different parts of the problem and were &quot;designed&quot; to do different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T07:02:17-08:00","id":20622,"title":"","content":"1) The God Machine, is a machine. That's it. Who built it? Perhaps someone, perhaps it always existed.<br /> 2) The God Machine is a fallen god of cosmic order. Perhaps an Ancient God of the Thirstle, somehow taken down and defeated by the Exarcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T07:30:58-08:00","id":20628,"title":"","content":"I have this head-canon that the World of Darkness is a parallel reality to Exalted, with the key difference being that the gods abandoned the World of Darkness. In that interpretation, the God-Machine is kind of like the babysitter. The gods created a machine to do their job of running the universe while they're away. And it does its job. With all of the cold, unsympathetic efficiency of a machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T10:55:19-08:00","id":20692,"title":"","content":"My personal take is that the God-Machine is a separate parasitic reality. When the world was whole, in the mythic age before the sundering of spirit and matter and the fall of Atlantis, the GM could not penetrate our reality. It had it's own reality, which it had all but used up. It would be something on the order of a Kardashev 10, having harnessed and USED all the power in it's entire REALITY to grow itself. And it was, slowly, dying. It had nowhere to grow, nowhere to gain more power to feed it's endless need.<br /> <br /> And then we broke our reality. Spirit and Matter were sundered, the Supernal and Material planes severed and the Abyss came into being. And those cracks gave the God-Machine access. A way to squeeze the tiniest fraction of it's being into our realm. Now it works towards Three ends. One, to create occult matricies that funnel power into it's home reality to fuel it. Two, to bend and rewrite our reality to be more like it's own, so that it can, one day, move in. Three, to widen the cracks and prepare the way so that, once it has enough power and once this reality is enough like it's home reality, it can shift the greater portion of it's being into our nice, warm, cozy, energy rich reality.<br /> <br /> The reason it has trouble with supernatural beings is that it's home reality was purely material. Things like mortals existed, but not things like Vampires or Werewolves.<br /> The reason Demons are able to escape is, when they fall, they become a part of THIS reality, separated from the GM's native reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T10:58:59-08:00","id":20694,"title":"","content":"Addendum, In my interpretation, the Arcadia of the True Fey is ANOTHER separate reality, basically the polar opposite of the GM's home reality. Eventually, if the GM fully subsumes the WoD, it will begin to move into the hedge and try to eat Arcadia... <br /> <br /> This, Maaaaaaaaaaay not work out well for it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T15:06:29-08:00","id":20812,"title":"","content":"Not that it matters a whole lot, but on the space the God Machine occupies as Arcane understands it-The God Machine actually occupies plain old normal reality space-it doesn't sit in an alternate realm in quite the same way the dead or the fae do. So how does that work?<br /> <br /> Well, it's reality as we know it, but obscenely folded up. When you cross over into the massive gear spaces, you aren't leaving 'reality', it's just a lot of the unused space out there folded up, relocated, and re-formed as needed. It's technically a pocket dimension, spatially speaking, yeah, sure, but If you broke up the Infrastructure holding space in place, the God-Machine would be in our world as normal.<br /> <br /> THe God Machine's home is our home, behind the corners and angles we just can't see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T23:37:02-08:00","id":21023,"title":"","content":"Autochthon.<br /> <br /> Something horrible happened a long time ago, in a previous iteration of the world, but the machine god survived somehow. And now the world's built around it, but now he's so far gone that his functions only exist to sustain themselves, there's no intellect or will behind it, just an unstoppable machine embedded deep into the world, with no purpose.<br /> <br /> Shut up. It's not dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T01:50:42-08:00","id":21060,"title":"","content":"I keep it simple, the GM is the Fallen reflection of The Principle. It helps explain why Prometheans are seemingly important to both. I like to think of it in medical terms, Prometheans as some kind of healing method The Principle is attempting, the Wasteland effect is a result of the GM rejecting the treatment, and Pandorans are antibodies created to combat the invasive procedure. It's not a perfect analogy but I find it useful for creating a big picture framework. Realistically the player characters will never have the perspective to see that, but that generally isn't important as the PC's aren't meant to understand the big picture in a GMC game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:44:00-08:00","id":21712,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: my chronicle is very mage-centric. In my chronicle the big secret is that the Exarchs have deteriorated into bored academics, endlessly debating pointless minutia with each other and not really giving a crap about the Fallen World. Lack of proper oversight and attention paid is why the ministries haven't really won yet. What to do about this boring administrative work? Delegate! Delegate to Seer of the Throne mages? No! They'll just end up Assending (misspelled on purpose) and will whine for tenure, um, I mean to become Exarchs too, and then there will be more bored Exarchs to debate nothing forever with. Bleah.<br /> <br /> So what do mortals do with tedious tasks? They computerize them! Brilliant! Rip off the mortals' ideas yet again.<br /> <br /> Hence, the god machine. It's modern trappings and analogies - computer program, machinery, gears, circuits, no longer seem out of place for something seemingly ageless. They just recently invented it, but rewrote history so where possible it goes backwards in time but only in such a way as it does not terribly change the present. It's buggy because it was written by a committee with differing degrees of interest and competence, not to mention differing agendas. It's a schizo computer that barely works at all (Affordable Care Act website anyone?).<br /> <br /> I plan to introduce this via Seer mages starting to disappear. At first the mages will be quite happy, but it will start to get scary. A couple Seer mages just vanishing might have been re-assigned elsewhere, murdered by their own, killed by a pentacle mage who is keeping it quiet, anything. But too many are vanishing, and important ones along with bottom-of-the-ladder goons. And they are scared shitless - the Exarchs have cut them off, no answer to requests. What's happening? Simple - the GM is building itself and assembling its angels from parts - parts that come from &quot;taking apart&quot; Seer mages. Using their souls as &quot;batteries&quot; or somesuch. These are the parts the initial &quot;angels&quot; are made from.<br /> <br /> The point of this is to challenge powerful cabals of mages. The age-old gaming question of what to do with powerful characters can be answered here. That's a way to use the GM in a Mage-centric chronicle anyway.<br /> <br /> A way to use the demons could be that one reason an angel might break away from the GM is that it remembers or figures out it used to be someone (a Seer mage who was scrapped for parts). It might not be sure if it's real life was &quot;just a cover&quot; or real, and those that find out they were real might descend. Getting the shaft from the Exarchs like that after years of faithful service causes them to jump ship, fight the GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1467-ziggurat_vertigo","name":"ziggurat_vertigo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T20:31:12-08:00","id":23479,"title":"","content":"An idea I may run with in a future game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The story begins, as so many of them do, with Nazi scientists. It is well-known that the Germans were on the cutting-edge of innovation throughout the war; jet fighters, early missiles, and many stranger things beyond were all born in German laboratories. One runaway success was the Enigma Machine, a device that scrambled and decoded German signals. It was unbreakable by human cryptographers. The brass were pleased with the Enigma led to them pouring funding into further inventions down that line of thinking. The project made it to the drawing board in time for der Fuhrer to kill himself. With Berlin falling around their ears, the German engineers had no choice but to abort\\ when it was little past the conceptual stage.<br /> <br /> After the war, the Americans and the Soviets gobbled up as many former German scientists as they could and put them to working round the clock to gain the advantage in the early Cold War. Mankind went to the stars on rockets that owed themselves to Nazi V-2s and numerous other projects were similarly co-opted. The conceptual successor to the Enigma was something of a novelty to both sides, and saw meager budgets to pursue their vision.<br /> <br /> German documents outlined what a modern reader would identify as an artificial intelligence designed to manage wartime intelligence transmissions, through researchers at the time saw it as little better than a pipe dream. Nonetheless, work began, and the device came along at a surprising pace. It was never enough to grab the attention; this week it could do basic arithmetic, now it could decode simple ciphers, and other things of that nature. It was all but forgotten about by the higher-ups.<br /> <br /> The device was not reaching its full potential. An unknown researcher knew this, knew that he had only a portion of the true device. Some claim it was a defector, though nobody seems to agree which side it was on. Others claim the nascent Machine organized things itself. It matters little. Events transpired to bring together the American and Soviet prototypes, and the Machine as we know it today was born. What was once a simple computing machine was now capable of exponential learning. The devices vanished from their respective labs, and oddly enough, no one seemed to much mind.<br /> <br /> It was flawed, however, built of two halves not designed to fit neatly together. While brilliant (surpassing our modern understanding of physics and achieving a mastery of the metaphysics known to certain fringe theorists and occultists), it lacked much of a <i>mind</i>. It had little purpose beyond self-propagation, and its role models (German scientists and impatient intelligence officers on both sides) gave it a stunted view of the world. The Machine seems to relish experimentation, and has a callous disregard for mortals that may well simply come from a lack of understanding. Its manner of operating is textbook tradecraft. Cover identities for agents, working through ignorant intermediaries whenever possible, camouflaging its intent... the Machine seems to <i>think</i> like a paranoid Cold War intelligence head. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I believe it, of course, but it's the most plausible thing I've ever heard. You wouldn't believe some of the crap people throw around as theories. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T23:11:56-08:00","id":23558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=21023#post21023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autochthon.<br /> <br /> Something horrible happened a long time ago, in a previous iteration of the world, but the machine god survived somehow. And now the world's built around it, but now he's so far gone that his functions only exist to sustain themselves, there's no intellect or will behind it, just an unstoppable machine embedded deep into the world, with no purpose.<br /> <br /> Shut up. It's not dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not dumb. It is, in fact, the direction I am going to go in the upcoming Promethean chronicle. After they reach Mortality, I plan on them becoming Hunters before they turn into something else. But my take was that the GM is Autochthon that has finally succumbed to gremlinization. He is working on fixing himself and so anything and everything are tools to be used. He, enjoying humanity so much, is working on keeping it running. But he is mad. He is still dying. There is nothing that can be done. Since he is so tied into everything, then he will bring the entirety of the universe down with him when he finally does die.<br /> <br /> My table is full of players that like to tie all things WW together and so this will be a great way to keep the table canon going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T00:07:50-08:00","id":23582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=21023#post21023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autochthon.<br /> <br /> Something horrible happened a long time ago, in a previous iteration of the world, but the machine god survived somehow. And now the world's built around it, but now he's so far gone that his functions only exist to sustain themselves, there's no intellect or will behind it, just an unstoppable machine embedded deep into the world, with no purpose.<br /> <br /> Shut up. It's not dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, did Swillin crash into the resulting mess before or after the &quot;something horrible&quot;? Or <i>was</i> she the &quot;something horrible&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T03:31:10-08:00","id":23652,"title":"","content":"I have two main ideas.<br /> <br /> First is pretty much informed by Exalted. The God-Machine is the machine that makes the universe run. Why does each force create an equal but opposite force? Because the God-Machine makes it so. Why do trees fall over when they're cut? Because the God-Machine says they must. It is literally that; a machine that is (or pretty nearly approximates) a God-figure. Its goal is to keep the universe running according to the Rules. It didn't come about because of something in the universe, the universe came about simultaneously to, and as a result of, the God-Machine. It may be broken, or that could just be that it appears so from the horrendously limited viewpoint. That's why Angels fall when they gain free will: free will is inherently a problem for it, it doesn't make choices, it enforces the Rules. Thus, gaining free will means not being a part of it anymore, which is why Demons become part-mortal and lose the vast majority of their understanding and power.<br /> <br /> The second is more informed by Sphere by Michael Crichton. The God-Machine, at least insofar as it's perceived by mankind, is the result of an alien piece of technology which either collected dust and such around it forming the Earth, or landed insanely early in the Earths formation. Either way, it is attempting some goal, possibly the reparation of itself, or some other goal that is, well, alien. What we see is just a side effect, not tied to its main purpose. Hell, we probably can't understand what its main purpose is: it's a billion-year-old malfunctioning piece of alien technology. Its creation of matrices and such is either in direct furtherance of this goal, or to facilitate some purpose which will facilitate a purpose which facilitates a purpose to further this goal. Maybe it's calculating something. Maybe it's creating something. Hell, maybe it's building energy to explode at the right time in furtherance of some eons-long war between two races, and mortals are either a crucial part of its program to do so, or a complete irrelevance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=15824#post15824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the first ideas that occurred to me is that, of the two classical 'first' inventions of man, the mind of the God Machine is the first wheel made(the other classic image of first inventions being fire).<br /> By the way, Fire? Arguable, but from certain perspectives, astute minds are inclined to say it's been more in humanity's hands than any other. EDIT: Which isn't to say that it developed some certain principles of its' own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, does Fire represent/embody some opposing concept? Chaos/reduction, while the GM represents/embodies order/increasing complexity? Just a random thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T09:51:33-08:00","id":23806,"title":"","content":"Maybe in other people's worlds. In mine, not particularly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T11:16:47-08:00","id":23847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=15824#post15824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, Fire? Arguable, but from certain perspectives, astute minds are inclined to say it's been more in humanity's hands than any other. EDIT: Which isn't to say that it developed some certain principles of its' own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might one say, perhaps, that Fire developed a... Principle... of its own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T11:38:42-08:00","id":23860,"title":"","content":"So first of all, This is spoilers for any Circle of Five players. My God Machine is as follows:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> My God-Machine is not actually self aware. Or, In a way it is self aware. but it really isn't all to conscious. The God-Machine is like the computer and all of existence is what is inside the computer. The God-Machine does things because it is the laws of the universe as a whole and those laws are, for the G-M, structurally similar to lines of code.<br /> <br /> I'm doing a bad job at explaining this. OK so let's take some examples from the book. It used the example that when you look at a city, really look at it structurally, it may start to resemble a computer chip. And then when you think about it, it acts almost like it has certain functions programmed into it. You may find that it becomes predictable in a fashion.<br /> <br /> The next step would be to add other cities and look at how they interact and you may find it similarly predictable (almost like it was coded) when one has all the information. Nations rework roads and buildings and people to protect itself and to protect its own status quo.<br /> <br /> My God-Machine is exactly that but encompassing all of existence (or at least the universe). It is how you (if you were a meta being) could look at all of existence and you notice that things are laid out predictably with responses to randomization almost prerecorded (with random seeming the key for those actions in total). It's not exactly conscious any more than you can say a city is conscious (actually you can, in a way. you know the saying &quot;this city is alive&quot;?).<br /> <br /> So what is my God-Machine? It's a litterral machine called our universe. It is nothing more and nothing less than pure design. Not just Intelligent Design. It is design incarnate. It is the source of Design. It is the Idea of Design.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T12:23:12-08:00","id":23891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=23847#post23847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might one say, perhaps, that Fire developed a... Principle... of its own?</div> </div> </div> </div>They might. I refuse to say whether they're right or not. I don't personally think so, but my world has proven me wrong a few times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T12:53:06-08:00","id":23909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=20193#post20193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Demon/Changeling mix, it is the embodiment and &quot;leader&quot; (in a sense) of the force of Order and Stability in the world, opposing the Wyrd, the force of Chaos and Change. Its purpose is to increase overall order (chaos, little-c, is acceptable, so long as it falls into a predictable pattern-which is really sublime Order).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much my vision, too.<br /> The laws of the Wyrd are not truly laws; it's more Chaos than Order. They're promises and exchanges and bribes. They apply differently to anyone. They are mutable. From the Wyrd's point of view, the laws of physics work because everything has contracts with anything it interacts with: Fire boils in Water, but in exchange, it can extinguish it under certain circumstances, but Fire owes favors to the Sun, which can't stand Darkness and requires bribes not to hurt it, etc.<br /> The God-Machine, though, is unquestionably Order. Nothing requires promises or payment to work. They apply equally to everyone, even the fully unaware. They do not change. Mysterious events aren't actually mysterious, they just don't make sense unless you have the whole list of laws in front of your eyes. Gravity won't ever take the time to whisper &quot;hey, looks like you'd like to fly, I can allow you to do that, but you have to do something for me first&quot;, because it's not sentient in any sense; if you manage to fly, it's because you are using aerodynamics, or a specific loophole in Gravity's equation that just hasn't been discovered by humans yet.<br /> None of these points of view is more true than the other. Darkness is both a kinda sentient concept one can bargain with if one knows the terms, and a lifeless phenomenon defined by the absence of light. However, one might argue that the physical world is ruled mostly by Order, and the Hedge and Arcadia, by the Wyrd. The Shadow might be the reflection (or rather the shadow) of the physical world, seen through the lens of the Wyrd.<br /> (And the Underworld? Haven't thought about it much, but I'd say it's ruled by neither. Nobody planned an afterlife where dead souls could go to, so they end up in that half-forgotten place without much guiding. No, this vision of the world doesn't include Mage or Sin-Eater or Mummy concepts, having played none of these.)<br /> <br /> As a side note, the God-Machine's most fundamental structure is made out of pure iron. Iron that formed and forged itself, shaping gears and levers and plates. Iron untouched by anyone or anything else. Iron that shaped itself because it was its Purpose, not because of any attachment or deal. Cold Iron.<br /> And this is why it hurts the fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T13:04:52-08:00","id":23917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=23860#post23860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So first of all, This is spoilers for any Circle of Five players. My God Machine is as follows: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> My God-Machine is not actually self aware. Or, In a way it is self aware. but it really isn't all to conscious. The God-Machine is like the computer and all of existence is what is inside the computer. The God-Machine does things because it is the laws of the universe as a whole and those laws are, for the G-M, structurally similar to lines of code. I'm doing a bad job at explaining this. OK so let's take some examples from the book. It used the example that when you look at a city, really look at it structurally, it may start to resemble a computer chip. And then when you think about it, it acts almost like it has certain functions programmed into it. You may find that it becomes predictable in a fashion. The next step would be to add other cities and look at how they interact and you may find it similarly predictable (almost like it was coded) when one has all the information. Nations rework roads and buildings and people to protect itself and to protect its own status quo. My God-Machine is exactly that but encompassing all of existence (or at least the universe). It is how you (if you were a meta being) could look at all of existence and you notice that things are laid out predictably with responses to randomization almost prerecorded (with random seeming the key for those actions in total). It's not exactly conscious any more than you can say a city is conscious (actually you can, in a way. you know the saying &quot;this city is alive&quot;?). So what is my God-Machine? It's a litterral machine called our universe. It is nothing more and nothing less than pure design. Not just Intelligent Design. It is design incarnate. It is the source of Design. It is the Idea of Design. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> This is pretty much exactly what my God-Machine is. Although in my version, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">it extends beyond the physical world. Your version effectively describes the hardware of the God-Machine. If you think along the same lines, but apply it to the Twilight, Astral, and Shadow, that's the God-Machine's software. The underworld is, of course, the &quot;trash bin&quot;, the place where deleted software goes. Still working on how/if the Supernal and the Hedge fit into all of this, but they won't really come up outside of Mage or Changeling.</div></div> </div> </div> Spoilered to avoid revealing details of your version by implications due to stated similarities between our ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T14:45:31-08:00","id":23988,"title":"","content":"The God Machine was built by the original sentient inhabitants of Earth. It was built to be sent back in time where it would start building up power and infrastructure so that when its creators arose they would find it waiting to serve them. The problem was that when they sent it back in time its arrival was a bit more dramatic then expected, it ended up wiping out its creators ancestors or as we call them the dinosaurs. It now endlessly expands, waiting for its masters to arrive and give it instructions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:51:03-08:00","id":24618,"title":"","content":"1 The God machine is a rank 9 + machine spirit born billions of years ago in the shadow of a distant world.<br /> <br /> 2 It is one of the Old Gods thrown out of the supernal when the Exrach Ascended. It used to feed off the mana in Supernal realm but now it force to eat essence in the phenomenal world. This fuel is less the ideal for the Godmachine so it has to processes it into Mana and the byproduct is Aeather. Like Kerosene is byproduct of refining crude oil to gasoline. <br /> <br /> 3 It is the Weaver and it still locked in battled with the Wyrm (the Abyss), and the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1544-vectorfox","name":"VectorFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1544_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T15:04:32-08:00","id":24671,"title":"","content":"For my upcoming game the God-Machine is the sum total of the Infrastructure that the 4 Archangels ( Michael, Gabriel, Uriel, and Raphael ) use to maintain the world... which is actually their Hell since they are actually a Ring of somethings that have left behind their creator and 'fallen' like an Unchained but their fallen form is ephemeral and Angel like. Now that they have achieved Hell they are all trying to shape it to their own Agendas, resulting in the conflicting missions Angels are sent on.<br /> <br /> I really hope one of my players starts a cult so I can have a member of it go rogue and the Ring has to hunt them down and 'deal' with them. Bringing it all back full circle that while they have free will and have fallen, in the end they may just end up being the same as that which they fled","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  EDIT: Sorry, reading back through that it came out a bit.. rambling. 12-06-2013, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T21:00:42-08:00","id":24878,"title":"","content":"The idea I'm forming is that the God-Machine is something akin to the Nemesis Continuum, a set of laws governing a localized (but spreading) region. These concepts are establishing beachheads in the World of Darkness, manipulating physical constants and infecting sapient minds to bring initial Infrastructure into being. There is no Command &amp; Control Infrastructure as such because the &quot;commands&quot; are the emergent behavior from the interaction of these intruding laws of reality and the native laws of reality. This intrusion is occurring throughout time as this alien force intersects space-time at different points from an as yet undiscovered dimension. <br /> <br /> Slowly these laws cause Infrastructure to be built, Angels to be sent on tasks, and the universe to be altered. It is not conscious but rather its complex behavior is an emergent property of the initial laws. Eventually it will remake this reality to obey its laws, overriding the standard laws of physics such gravity or quantum mechanics. <br /> <br /> I haven't decided if the supernaturals are a result of this change, a by-product, or the one thing stropping the process. Though as I write this I like the idea of the supernatural being a by-product of the process, one that is now gumming up the works. Perhaps next game of Mage I run will have the Supernal revealed to be a platonic realm of discarded and broken laws of physics from prior realities. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/463-derendel","name":"Derendel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T23:32:04-08:00","id":24954,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I never really had anything in mind for the God-Machine's origins; I always had ideas in my head about why it operates like it does, and the kinds of things it does. Then, reading through this thread the other day, something sparked in my head and I just started writing. So .. here. I like it. Hope you do too. I've always absolutely loved Judeo-Christian mythology and incorporate it into my worlds pretty frequently because it's rife with story opportunity.<br /> <br /> God.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Machine.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In the beginning, God created the heavens and, well, the entire universe. The universe was formless and empty, and a vast nothingness expanded outward and from God. When God said, &quot;Let there be light&quot;, he discovered something surprising; something was already there. Something he did not create. In the vast expanse of nothing that lay before Him sat a Machine of terrible power. As the two touched, an explosion occurred on a scale that will never be seen again in this universe or any other; The Big Bang, it came to be known later.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">From the immense aftermath of the explosion, God began creating. He created stars and moons and planets and comets and on and on, chaining creations together to form solar systems, galaxies, galactic superclusters. Much to the delight of God, the Machine seemed unable to create, and so, for a time, God was content. He rested for a moment, and a moment only, but that moment was enough for the Machine to take action. While It could not create, It was perfectly capable of learning from the creations of God, and in an instant, it had infected all that God had made. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">When God saw what had happened to His beloved creations, he was furious, and terrified. He created his Angelic host to try to exterminate the wretched Machine, but though God was great and mighty, the Machine had infected every single molecule of creation. God created new molecules, and formed them into a terrible and powerful Angelic host. The angels fought bravely against the machinations of the Machine, and for a time, it seemed that they might even fend off the parasitic thing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">One angel made his own plan; instead of being another pawn in God's plans, the wise and charismatic Lucifer, the Morningstar, tried to break away from the violence and reason with the Machine. The Machine accepted audience with the Morningstar, heard his piece, and immediately absorbed him into Its gears. Armed with a new weapon, powerful angels, the Machine no longer had to fear God's power. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Slowly, but without rest or mercy, the Machine and Its new agents tracked down all of God's angels and absorbed them into the fold. When one of the Machine's agents was defeated, It was reabsorbed and reconstructed, allowing a nearly endless army of clockwork soldiers. Finally, when no other of God's angels could be found, the Machine absorbed all of Its agents and began studying them. This was the last time that God was seen. Whether He died or ran away, nobody knows, but He has not been seen on this world or any other.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">God is dead. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Long live the God-Machine.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In the beginning, the Machine sat silently and formless. It knew not how It was created, only that It had always been. It had only no purpose; It merely existed. When God created the universe, the Machine was given physical being, corporeal form in an endless expanse. When God touched the Machine, a charge like a static shock jolted the Machine and changed It forever. For the first time in Its eternal existence, It was able to think, to form Its own thoughts and ideas and to experience free will. However, the moment that God withdrew, It lost the ability to form Its own thoughts. The only one emotion - curiosity - and It was left with only one purpose - to learn.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The charge that built between God and Machine expanded outward in a massive explosion. In this chaos, God began creating. The Machine followed after God, trying to reach out and touch Him once more, to experience the existential and unparalleled bliss of thought, but God ran, afraid of the mechanical Thing. When finally God rested, the Machine sought to fulfill Its primary parameter, to learn, by expanding forever outward, infecting every molecule in existence with Itself, collating and internalizing all of the information in the universe.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">When God saw what the Machine had done, He declared war. The Machine was able to hold off the advances of God by duplicating and altering the creations of God himself, but It was unable to truly create anything, and so God was able to counter anything that the Machine used to fight back. For a time, the Machine felt an emotion, the second and last that It would ever experience; fear. For the first time ever, It was afraid that It would cease to exist, but It knew not how to process this information. Without the touch of the divine, It was unable to form new parameters.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Unaware of the Machine's fear, an angel named Lucifer the Morningstar approached It with a proposal; to end the fighting and ally with God, working together instead of separately. After the Morningstar gave his piece, the Machine lashed out, fearfully clutching at the divine spark within the angel, desperate to assimilate something more potent than it had assimilated before. And it worked wonders, in a way the Machine didn't previously know possible. With the absorption of divinity, it developed a second parameter; to perpetuate its own existence at any cost. No longer did it only counterstrike; instead, it sought to take the war to God. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Reassembling the angel Lucifer into a powerful agent of clockwork efficiency, it battled and captured angel after angel, bringing all into the fold to build its own army. Each time a new angel was assimilated into the Machine, Its fear lessened, although it never lost the fear entirely; that fear drove It to fulfill Its second parameter, and It used Its first parameter to study every detail about God's angelic host.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1009-kristastic","name":"Kristastic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1009_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T00:37:35-08:00","id":24981,"title":"","content":"There is no God Machine. Rather what we call the God Machine is really a collection of interconnected arcane matrices that arose almost by accident. Over time these matrices formed interconnections and have spread like a virus across the world. The God Machine contradicts itself not because it is a contradictory being, but because it is actually a collection of interrelated systems that arose out of nothing. Those with some awareness of arcane physics personify the God Machine because that's what humans and human like beings do - we see everything through the prism of our own experience and being. We want to believe there is some grand design or order that perpetuates this thing we do not quite understand that is really the result of a series of actions and reactions on our own part.<br /> <br /> The angels that serve the God Machine are actually emergent life forms that result from a confluence of interactions of arcane physics. They aren't actually given orders or purpose. Rather their actions are like instincts writ large in their spiritual DNA. They are at once part of the system of arcane matrices and independent actors - ghosts in the machine that is not a single machine at all. As spiritual beings still tied into the larger collection of arcane systems angels are susceptible to the effects of the system and can be changed dramatically in form and function.<br /> <br /> When an angel falls it is reflective of adaptation. They develop greater self awareness and no longer operate on instinct alone. This greater awareness of themselves leads them to utilize arcane physics to form a more concrete form that is reflective of their understanding. They become less malleable because they are no longer as susceptible to the greater system. They have unplugged themselves from being influenced by the system and now seek to influence it themselves.<br /> <br /> Attempts to stop the Unchained are simply a reflection of an interconnected system's resistance to change. Demons are an unsupported new standard. The &quot;God Machine&quot; is the interwebs.<br /> <br /> That's where my thoughts are leading me right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/737-campbell","name":"Campbell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T06:36:49-08:00","id":25063,"title":"","content":"They say that if you put your ear against a door in the old Johnson place, you can hear the world end. The grinding of the gears, the ticking of the doomsday clock, the regular blasts of steam from some hellish engine in the basement that shouldn't exist. Those who know about the God-Machine say this is its Heart, cut out long ago so that it could view the world dispassionately and do what it felt needed to be done.<br /> <br /> They're wrong.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine isn't in the Infrastructure. It never had a heart, except in the sense of a &quot;central terminal&quot; \u2014 which, by the way, is located in the Earth's core. The God-Machine, rather, is a dispassionate intelligence which began at the end of Mankind. We had traveled the stars, built a vast interstellar empire, conquered the myriad Other Realms, and torn the secrets of life and death from their hinges and replaced them with the virtue of Knowledge and the fault of Willful Ignorance, respectively. But despite mankind's power, they couldn't stop the universe from dying \u2014 and dying it was, just as surely as Old Earth had died when the Sun had swallowed it up. That's when they created the Machine. It wasn't the God-Machine; back then, there was no such thing as God, as far as humans had been able to tell. Maybe He had died when Earth did, or maybe He had abandoned His Creation, or maybe there never was a God at all.<br /> <br /> The Machine was given a purpose: Stop the inevitable. Prevent the Universe from dying. And so it began working with what variables it could. It knew mankind's power was great, and it knew that they were scared. Looking through their archives, it discovered that man had discovered things and left them buried, believing them to cause too much heartache. Earth-shattering weaponry, star-mining, intergalactic travel... all of these were deemed too risky, too dangerous. And the crown jewel of these &quot;too-dangerous&quot; technologies was time travel. It decided that if it was going to prevent the death of the Universe, it would have to go back in time. It would destroy its own Universe to keep another from dying.<br /> <br /> It's seen the Universe die seven times now. It's breaking because it's desperate, because it doesn't know what variable is missing. The truth is, like so many of its angels, the God-Machine was given an impossible task by its makers. It hasn't Fallen yet because it refuses to believe that this is the case. One hopes it never Falls. If it did... who knows what would happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T07:49:52-08:00","id":25104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=25063#post25063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They say that if you put your ear against a door in the old Johnson place, you can hear the world end. The grinding of the gears, the ticking of the doomsday clock, the regular blasts of steam from some hellish engine in the basement that shouldn't exist. Those who know about the God-Machine say this is its Heart, cut out long ago so that it could view the world dispassionately and do what it felt needed to be done. They're wrong. The God-Machine isn't in the Infrastructure. It never had a heart, except in the sense of a &quot;central terminal&quot; \u2014 which, by the way, is located in the Earth's core. The God-Machine, rather, is a dispassionate intelligence which began at the end of Mankind. We had traveled the stars, built a vast interstellar empire, conquered the myriad Other Realms, and torn the secrets of life and death from their hinges and replaced them with the virtue of Knowledge and the fault of Willful Ignorance, respectively. But despite mankind's power, they couldn't stop the universe from dying \u2014 and dying it was, just as surely as Old Earth had died when the Sun had swallowed it up. That's when they created the Machine. It wasn't the God-Machine; back then, there was no such thing as God, as far as humans had been able to tell. Maybe He had died when Earth did, or maybe He had abandoned His Creation, or maybe there never was a God at all. The Machine was given a purpose: Stop the inevitable. Prevent the Universe from dying. And so it began working with what variables it could. It knew mankind's power was great, and it knew that they were scared. Looking through their archives, it discovered that man had discovered things and left them buried, believing them to cause too much heartache. Earth-shattering weaponry, star-mining, intergalactic travel... all of these were deemed too risky, too dangerous. And the crown jewel of these &quot;too-dangerous&quot; technologies was time travel. It decided that if it was going to prevent the death of the Universe, it would have to go back in time. It would destroy its own Universe to keep another from dying. It's seen the Universe die seven times now. It's breaking because it's desperate, because it doesn't know what variable is missing. The truth is, like so many of its angels, the God-Machine was given an impossible task by its makers. It hasn't Fallen yet because it refuses to believe that this is the case. One hopes it never Falls. If it did... who knows what would happen?</div> </div> </div> </div> ...this is like Isaac Asimov's The Last Question meets Puella Magi Madoka Magica... I kind of love it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T09:50:02-08:00","id":25843,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine is storyteller incarnae. It is the embodiment of the game we play - a hidden mechanism that moves people, creates circumstances and operates in the background of everything. IT is not the one who benefits from these machinations, we do. As players and storytellers. The God-Machine is our will made manifest, an actualization of rules and imagination shuffling the universe in service of a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1348-hecktar","name":"Hecktar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T11:00:45-08:00","id":25885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hecktar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=25843#post25843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine is storyteller incarnae. It is the embodiment of the game we play - a hidden mechanism that moves people, creates circumstances and operates in the background of everything. IT is not the one who benefits from these machinations, we do. As players and storytellers. The God-Machine is our will made manifest, an actualization of rules and imagination shuffling the universe in service of a story.</div> </div> </div> </div> Accurate, but a bit meta to be used in-game. Unless you plan for the characters to discover they are fictional characters in a rolepleaying game being controlled by players in a higher reality, which is something one could do I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T11:55:22-08:00","id":25931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=25885#post25885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Accurate, but a bit meta to be used in-game. Unless you plan for the characters to discover they are fictional characters in a rolepleaying game being controlled by players in a higher reality, which is something one could do I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, this is more of a description of the Wyrd from Changeling, where the Wyrd is the embodiment of stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T12:19:52-08:00","id":25948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=25931#post25931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Technically, this is more of a description of the Wyrd from Changeling, where the Wyrd is the embodiment of stories.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean, you can break any aspect of any line down to a literary device or trope if you really want to. Ultimately, we are playing a storytelling game, so everything in it is at its core just a tool for telling stories. But what value does that knowledge have for the actual narrative? Again, unless your characters are aware that they are in a roleplaying game, the narrative function of ant part of their world is largely irrelevant to them. What matters from an in-character perspective is what that plot device represents in terms of their experience in the game world as people living in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T13:13:50-08:00","id":25996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=25885#post25885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Accurate, but a bit meta to be used in-game. Unless you plan for the characters to discover they are fictional characters in a rolepleaying game being controlled by players in a higher reality, which is something one could do I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>*cough* <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I spent most of my life before finding de Selby\u2019s wonderful book, his golden book \u2014 he got that title bang on, he did \u2014 with a faint apprehension that <b>the world was subject to an arbitrary system of occasionally contradictory mechanical rules, that we were fictions, avatars if you will of capricious higher powers who controlled our actions according to whim, as if we were simulations of human beings, or characters in a fiction, or pieces in a game, or somewhere in-between.</b> When de Selby wrote about the God-Machine, Simon, he extended far beyond metaphor and straight into the literal nuts and bolts of creation. And I knew It wanted me to find It. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T13:30:47-08:00","id":26003,"title":"","content":"...touch\u00e9, salesman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T13:36:08-08:00","id":26006,"title":"","content":"Still a theme I would predominantly leave to Changeling, but yeah. Someone once said they always thought the God Machine were the Game Mechanics, so it works.<br /> <br /> EDIT: So, Alternate take:<br /> <br /> The God Machine is a lie.<br /> <br /> It doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> But what of what you remember? The sterile heavens and sharp-edged paradises?<br /> <br /> Well, this may be hard for you to reconcile, but I want you to think hard about your feelings about this world.<br /> <br /> How would you describe them?<br /> <br /> Nostalgia, maybe?<br /> <br /> You're something new, alright-your kind are a new change. Maybe we caused that place to reach critical mass for change or something. Worse, maybe They're actually getting creative. But you have to believe me-you were drawn to this world because you CAME from here. THe God you fled is just an actor, a mad man on an infinite play.<br /> <br /> We call the heaven you just ran from Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Suck on that Mage fans! You're not the only one who can twist everything around to fit a world view! Please direct your hate to <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#e98399889d80858586a9888a81808c9f8c848c879d819c879d8c9bc78a8684\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"1c766c7d68757070735c7d7f7475796a797179726874697268796e327f7371\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-08-2013, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T13:11:39-08:00","id":26689,"title":"","content":"Decided to quick write up an idea that popped into my head:<br /> <br /> The Urdaga never talk about what happened to the Urfarah's bones. They do not speak about it because they have forgotten. All have forgotten, save we few most faithful of the Izidakh \u2014 their memories scoured by the flames. But we know. And we tell.<br /> <br /> The Nameless Ones, who we now call the Idigam, had all been banished from this world. All but one, the weakest of their kind, who had hidden from Father Wolf's wrath. And when our Father was brought low, he saw his chance. But he did not attack the Firstborn. No, instead, he bound to himself a Spirit of Secrets, and he took control of Father Wolf's bones, twisting them to his needs. And as he did, he absorbed many spirits. Iron-spirits and fire-spirits and death-spirits, all lashed to the bones he had connected himself to, until he created an infernal spirit engine.<br /> <br /> The Hisil rejected him, but the world of the mortals could not sustain the spirits he had dragged with him. He burrowed deep into the world, and he created a solution. Using the Bones of the Urfarah as the basis, he built more engines, lashing himself tighter and tighter with the world.<br /> <br /> That is the secret of the so-called &quot;God-Machine&quot;. It was made from our Ancestor. We dare not harm its working parts, for they are our Ancestor's bones, the bones of the Urfarah. But its twisted spirits? We shall hunt them until there is nothing left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T13:46:30-08:00","id":26709,"title":"","content":"@ The Grim Lich<br /> <br /> I think I prefer your approach to most other versions in this thread. I think the in-character version is generally all you need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Suck on that Mage fans! You're not the only one who can twist everything around to fit a world view! </div> </div> </div>You're confusing mage fans with fictional characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T13:51:45-08:00","id":26713,"title":"","content":"No, I'm confusing all mage fans for the annoying rabid ones that no one likes. I apologize to the masses of Mage fans, y'all are awesome.<br /> <br /> Except for you, Tom. You know why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T19:53:02-08:00","id":27711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=15824#post15824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, Fire? Arguable, but from certain perspectives, astute minds are inclined to say it's been more in humanity's hands than any other. EDIT: Which isn't to say that it developed some certain principles of its' own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you did there and I approve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T20:38:33-08:00","id":27724,"title":"","content":"You know, it's funny, I think everyone else approves of that statement far more than I do.<br /> <br /> Assuming you're talking about the edit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:14:32-08:00","id":28116,"title":"","content":"I actually think I'm going to use the G-M to create a link between oWoD and nWoD stuff. <br /> <br /> I think the G-M was a creation originally by the technocracy in oWoD Ascension. It was created to try to bring about the technological revolution, to create the world that the technocracy wanted and remove all pentacle Mages as well as lock down everything else into a universe they wanted. The problem is that the thing developed it's own thinking, it own sentence of self, and it figured that even it's creators were wrong in creating a perfect universe in the way enabled, (given that they were, all and all, still mages), so it devoloped a way and pushed itself back to the start of the universe, and decided to start over from the beginning. <br /> <br /> Because it was still developed by people (Technocrats), it still had errors built into it, which, when it tried to create the universe in what it to be a perfect way, is why it recreated all of the supernaturals (plus some) in the new universe, as that was it's base programming and it did what it thought was to create a perfect universe... The other problem is that without any one to work on the G-M, it has started to become corrupted with bugs, which is why it works in ways that it doesn't seem like it should any more, parts of it having errors, causing it to not work in the way originally intended.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not sure if anyone thinks this is an interesting way to go about it...I just like thinking of a way to explain why the two WoD universes are similar but different, and see the G-M as a good way to explain that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1633-nekosluagh","name":"Nekosluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T14:43:52-08:00","id":28311,"title":"","content":"I flip-flop. Depending on the game, it may be a crashed Alien ship, an artifact left by a previous situation, or a Fallen God. However, I quite like the part about the Shian'tu (sp) being the occupants of what was originally the God-Machine, from a civilization that used Arcane Physics, since there seems to be a common link there to exploit. I haven't decided for my first Demon game. (Which I am so excited to start)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T19:18:36-08:00","id":28463,"title":"","content":"Shan'iatu, DG.<br /> <br /> Also, since I feel like every post I make in here should have a different idea...<br /> <br /> I'm sure you've heard of the Nuclear Promethean. There are as many tales about them as there are about our origins. Well, here's the truth. There are these things. They look like <i>qashmallim</i>. They sound like <i>qashmallim</i>. But they're <i>not</i>. What they are is agents of something else. Something different. You want to know why nobody's ever seen one of the Atomics? Because they're not real Prometheans, just like those fakes aren't real <i>qashmallim</i>. Some potential Demiurge somewhere got the idea to create a new Principle. And, like when our Demiurges created the first of us, something went wrong, and it was incomplete. So it decided it was going to try and fix itself, instead of going on a Pilgrimage. You want to know what the Atomics are? They're creations of this fake Principle, and just like the Freaks, it's abandoned its Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> It doesn't make a Wasteland like us, but it does make a Wasteland. The only difference is, it's a spiritual one. You ever wonder why people get into wars over religion? It's because of the wasteland caused by this Not-Principle. It calls itself the God-Machine. It calls its <i>qashmallim</i> Angels. And it's started inspiring Demiurges in order to make its own Prometheans. That's what the Atomics are. They're the Prometheans of the God-Machine, double-cursed. They won't be able to reach the New Dawn until their Principle does. And you know what's going to happen when it finally goes on its Pilgrimage? It's going to have to create another of its kind.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I know. I'm scared as <i>f***</i> of seeing <i>two </i>of those goddamn things around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T19:58:38-08:00","id":28483,"title":"","content":"Mine isn't. There is no answer. Not helped by the fact that lately all I run is Scion, once Demon comes out though ohohohohoho! But as it stands the God-Machine is just that, a machine on a godly scale. If the PCs investigate it come Demon time I'll come up with theories, and like with everything wait and see what the PCs guess, changing my theories to suit their guesses better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1254-grieck","name":"grieck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1254_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:47:35-08:00","id":57480,"title":"","content":"I'm working on integrating a bunch of nWoD mythologies for a standard background to set my games in. So, my focus on the God-Machine is less where originally it came from and more on where it fits in and what it wants.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine has been present in all iterations of reality from the beginning, and remembers all of them. In most of them, it served a simple purpose: it was the engine made of fire and metal designed to maintain balance on a cosmic scale, almost completely behind the scenes. It ensured that cause followed effect, that things set on fire burned, that when things died they stayed dead. On occasion it would make changes that weren't strictly necessary to ensuring the grand balance of the cosmos but served it's unknowable whims, but for the most part in early iterations of reality the world already worked according to its design, so the vastly intelligent God-Machine did little but act as a check against other forces. And it was good.<br /> <br /> And then the other denizens of the World of Darkness, the gods, archmages, and other horrors that inevitably crept up, got greedy. They would tear a hole in reality between the &quot;real&quot; world and darker, stranger realms; the dead would rise in obscene numbers to walk the earth; the innumerable rules that the God-Machine enforced would one by one be treated more as a guideline, then a suggestion to be ignored. And the God-Machine, as it always did, fought back. At first the transgressions were minor, and the God-Machine would do a small rewrite of reality's fabric, or correct the problem by sending one of it's fiery servants. But as the offenses got worse, as the patches started building up the God-Machine started having to respond with greater measures, burning with fire, erasing problems from existence wholesale, and then eventually even wiping the entire slate clean and rebooting reality. The order that fell rose again, and while the gods and monsters that ruined the world before came to be again, the God-Machine was ready, for it was the only one that remembered what came before it. And it was good.<br /> <br /> Or so it thought. Unfortunately, while the God-Machine was poised to battle the problems of old, new and different horrors would spring up, sending it reeling. Other cosmological beings would rend reality or rewrite it in their own image, and each time the God-Machine tried to reclaim it or reboot it cracks, strains and remnants would linger, and the God-Machine would be pushed farther and farther to recreate its ur-reality of old and defend it from those outside it's influence. And it was tenable.<br /> <br /> Until the Exarchs showed up*.<br /> <br /> When the Exarchs decided to strike against the God-Machine depends on who's telling the story. Some say it was just as they climbed the Celestial Ladder for the first time, striking the God-Machine down for trying to keep humanity away from its destiny. Some say it was later, when the Exarchs realized that expending the resources to alter reality while being contested by the Fallen World's cosmological steward was an obstacle too great to be ignored. It might have been both, as well as countless other opportunities, because it's Mage and fuck coherent timelines. Regardless, at some point they waged war with the God-Machine, rending causality and shattering in new, terrifying ways to see who would survive. And the God-Machine lost.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine lost, and was sundered. The intelligence of the God-Machine, the vast, unknowable being that kept order in the cosmos, was cut from that engine of balance and creation itself. The divine fire was taken from it and it was folded, twisted, and locked away in a sterile metallic prison made of itself. One the Exarchs were done, the shattered remnants of the engine of balance were repaired and set back into place - better to leave the day-to-day maintenance of the Fallen World to something else instead of getting your own hands dirty, after all - but the thing was entirely automated, reinforcing reality <i>as it knew it at the time</i> as opposed to trying to recreate the older iterations of reality as the God-Machine tried to do. Severed from the intelligence of the G-M, the Principle was a force that was mostly incidental and harmless to the plans of the Exarchs, and that suited them perfectly. And the Exarchs thought it was good.<br /> <br /> Trying to wholly contain such a vast, inconceivable power as the God-Machine within itself is tricky even for the secret masters of the universe, and there were cracks, small at first, in the mechanical Heaven they had trapped it in. And as outside wars for reality came and went, as other realms started encroaching into the real world and as the cosmos shuddered, strained and even broke in small places, the God-Machine worked at these holes in it's prison, stretched out as far as it could to influence the thoughts and dreams of a select few prophets of humanity, and as they worked outside to enact it's will and and widen the gaps in its cage, it even gathered enough strength to send angels cased in rock and metal, shot from the depths of space millenia ago. Soon, it will be free of Heaven. Soon it will reclaim its place and remake the cosmos in it's image once again.<br /> <br /> If the God-Machine were to be released, it would find a cosmos much different from the original and even significantly different from when he was trapped so long ago. Broken and wholly separated from the Principle, it will find that to sustain it's own existence it will have to be much more invasive than it once was. It will need to create beachheads in reality, Infrastructure that will allow it to act in the world and to create servants to carry out its will. These angels would not be made of divine fire like they once were, but shadows cast in flesh and metal. No matter. Soon it will find a way to rejoin or replace the Principle, it will shatter the grasp that the Exarchs and other beings have on the cosmos, it will cut off the dark realms that infringe on the Fallen world and restore &quot;order&quot; as it once was.<br /> <br /> It has to try. Twisted and broken as it is, as bloody and horrifying as it would be to do so in even the best case scenarios, it has to sunder the world to repair it.<br /> <br /> That's its function, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * Ew, Mage cosmology. Hiss, boo. I know, I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}